      en: "Assam Tea Gardens is a notable landmark in the Indian state of Assam. Assam is the largest tea-producing state in India. The region is known for its strong, malty black tea. Regionally it captures the diversity and complexity of this part of India. Several characteristic features stand out: Assam tea is enjoyed worldwide. The tea industry is a major employer. In this sense, Assam Tea Gardens is one of the characteristic examples of Assam and of India as a whole. Society K7 — Daily life, customs and ways of living in India."
